      "content": "UNION AND ITS TERRITORY"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Part I of the Indian Constitution encompasses Articles 1 to 4, dealing with the Union and its Territory.",
        "Article 1 defines the name and territory of India.",
        "Article 2 governs the admission or establishment of new states.",
        "Article 3 empowers Parliament regarding the formation of new states and alteration of areas, boundaries, or names of existing states.",
        "The States Reorganisation Act of 1956 reshaped state boundaries and established Union Territories."
      ],
